175→        <div class="project-area">
176→          <div class="area-header">
177→            <span class="area-name">Checkpoint &amp; Squash Merge System</span>
178→            <span class="area-count">~18 sessions</span>
179→          </div>
180→          <div class="area-desc">Core feature work on checkpoint ordering, squash-merge rewind/resume behavior, checkpoint generation rotation, and v1/v2 checkpoint separation planning. Claude was used to analyze existing restore logic, implement ordering fixes, build resume support, resolve merge conflicts across 51 files, extract shared helpers, and produce design documentation and RFDs.</div>
181→        </div>
182→      
183→        <div class="project-area">
184→          <div class="area-header">
185→            <span class="area-name">Git Operations &amp; Branch Management</span>
186→            <span class="area-count">~12 sessions</span>
187→          </div>
188→          <div class="area-desc">Various git workflow tasks including selective reverts, branch cleanup, merge conflict resolution, creating feature branches with structured commits, and investigating metadata branch behavior. Claude handled both routine operations and complex scenarios like recovering from accidental hard resets and tracing commit trailer code paths.</div>
189→        </div>
190→      
191→        <div class="project-area">
192→          <div class="area-header">
193→            <span class="area-name">CLI Tooling &amp; Extensions</span>
194→            <span class="area-count">~10 sessions</span>
195→          </div>
196→          <div class="area-desc">Work on CLI features including single channel/playlist download support, oh-my-zsh plugin exploration, an &apos;entire update&apos; command design, E2E CI test debugging/triage, and a Firefox extension port attempt. Claude was used for codebase analysis, feature implementation with tests, and CI failure diagnosis, though the Firefox porting effort hit repeated friction with incompatible approaches.</div>
197→        </div>
